{"name":"Honey Bunny","hex":"#dbb881","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"honey bunny","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of honeybunny."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/honey_bunny"}],"entries":[{"title":"Honey Bunny (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Honey Bunny is a 2026 drama film written, and directed by Igor Jelinović in his debut feature. A co-production between Croatia and Serbia the film follows a battle that brews between middle-aged sisters over ownership of a holiday home on the Croatian island of Hvar in the Adriatic Sea."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b0/Honey_Bunny_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey_Bunny_(film)","wikidata":"Q140851149"},{"title":"Lola Bunny","blocks":[{"text":"Lola Bunny is a Looney Tunes cartoon character portrayed as an anthropomorphic female rabbit created by Warner Bros. Pictures. She is generally depicted as Bugs Bunny's girlfriend. She first appeared in the 1996 film Space Jam."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Lola_Bunny_Space_Jam_svg.svg/330px-Lola_Bunny_Space_Jam_svg.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lola_Bunny","wikidata":"Q1575844"},{"title":"Honey","blocks":[{"text":"Honey is a sweet and viscous substance made by several species of bees, the best-known of which are honey bees. Honey is made and stored to nourish bee colonies. Bees produce honey by gathering and then refining the sugary secretions of plants or the secretions of other insects, like the honeydew of aphids. This refinement takes place both within individual bees, through regurgitation and enzymatic activity, and during storage in the hive, through water evaporation that concentrates the honey's sugars until it is thick and viscous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cc/Runny_hunny.jpg/330px-Runny_hunny.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honey","wikidata":"Q10987"},{"title":"Rabbit","blocks":[{"text":"Rabbits, or bunnies, are small mammals in the family Leporidae, which is in the order Lagomorpha. They are familiar throughout the world as a small herbivore, a prey animal, a domesticated form of livestock, and a pet, having a widespread effect on ecologies and cultures. The most widespread rabbit genera are Oryctolagus and Sylvilagus. The former, Oryctolagus, includes the European rabbit, Oryctolagus cuniculus, which is the ancestor of the hundreds of breeds of domestic rabbit and has been introduced on every continent except Antarctica. The latter, Sylvilagus, includes over 13 wild rabbit species, among them the cottontails and tapetis. Wild rabbits not included in Oryctolagus and Sylvilagus include several species of limited distribution, including the pygmy rabbit, volcano rabbit, and Sumatran striped rabbit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Oryctolagus_cuniculus_Rcdo.jpg/330px-Oryctolagus_cuniculus_Rcdo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rabbit","wikidata":"Q9394"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Britt_McKillip_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Britt_McKillip_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Britt_McKillip_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Britt_McKillip_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABritt_McKillip_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Kristin_Wiig_2013.jpg/500px-Kristin_Wiig_2013.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.